; A declaration-macro invocation INSIDE an imported module generates
; declarations in that module's namespace (MAC-EXP-16, 2026-08-15,
; where the v1 surface refused it as AX3027). What is left to refuse
; is the visibility question, and it is the same one a hand-written
; declaration answers: the template's own `pub` decides whether the
; product leaves the module.
;
; `insideModule` comes from a `pub` template and is nameable here;
; `hiddenInside` does not, so naming it is AX3023 - the same
; diagnostic, with the same wording, that a private hand-written
; declaration draws. The module's own call to it still works, which
; is what makes this a visibility rule rather than a deletion.
(import DeclIn)

(:: main Int)

(fn (main) (+ (+ touch insideModule) hiddenInside))
